  "notes": [
    "The two cabinet floor images are independent: protect cabinet polygons in the final world art, but retain the clean generated plate under their old footprints for runtime cleanup.",
    "Subtract every opaque pixel in every foreground atlas part, including appended wall masks and marked foreground entries, after applying these floor polygons.",
    "Keep current layer strokes, collision, object positions and disco/light logic unchanged.",
    "Release76 authorization extends the shiny surface through the nightclub passage and purple perimeter, right up to the preserved colored dance tiles.",
    "Use the pinned release75 floor plate everywhere outside plateEditPolygons so the already-approved main hall remains byte-identical.",
    "foregroundFloorCuts identify existing atlas alpha that contains floor rather than fixtures. Clear those alpha pixels in a new derived atlas and exclude them from background preservation.",
    "The main-counter apron is duplicated in its neighboring plant atlas mask. Both cuts are needed to avoid repainting the old tile patch over the cleaned background.",
    "The colored dance-floor boundary comes from dance-floor.js VERTEX_ROWS with a narrow outward rim. Its tile artwork and interaction coordinates must not change."
  ],
